# Cloudflare reads this file from the export root (`expo export` copies public/
# into dist/), and Workers Static Assets honours it for every asset response.
#
# Why it has to exist: Cloudflare PAGES added these two headers to every response
# on its own, and Workers Static Assets does not (~/Oxy/docs/infra-and-deploys.md,
# "Pages ADDS x-content-type-options…"). Without them a browser may sniff a
# declared Content-Type into a script. Declaring them here makes them a property
# of this deployment rather than of the platform. The deploy workflow asserts
# both on the live origin after every deploy.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Content-hashed: every file the Expo export writes under /_expo/static/ is named
# by a hash of its bytes, so a browser keeps it for a year and never revalidates.
# The asset server's default (`max-age=0, must-revalidate`) made every return
# visit re-ask for each one. Entry files (index.html, public/) keep that default.
#
# Known limit: this app has no Worker, and `not_found_handling` answers a hashed
# name this deploy lacks (an old tab asking for the last release's chunk) with
# index.html, which this rule then marks immutable too. Alia's and Clarity's
# Workers turn that miss into an uncached 404; one here would be its own change.
/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
